{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgApFXRLFjxxbGKw5DUWQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night; it just dies before it can tell you anything. `launchctl print` shows 6 runs, each ending with exit code 1, and the error log has the same two lines for every run:\n\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\n**Causes** (written up in `ANSWER.md`):\n\n1. **Why you got no failure note:** the script does `status=$?`, but in zsh `status` is a built-in variable you can't assign to (it's another name for `$?`). Trying to assign it is a fatal error, so zsh stops at line 19 and the call to `notify.sh` with the failure message never runs. A successful run would have died there too. I confirmed this with `zsh -c 'false; status=$?; echo after'`, which prints the error and never prints `after`. **Fixed** by renaming the variable to `rc`.\n2. **Why it failed:** `claude` isn't logged in when launchd runs it. launchd doesn't load your shell startup files, so credentials set up for your normal terminal aren't available to the 02:30 run. The script now loads `~/.config/nightly-review/env` if that file exists. **You need to create it once:** run `claude setup-token`, put `export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=...` in that file, and `chmod 600` it. I'd also put `TG_BOT_TOKEN` there so `notify.sh` doesn't have to reach the keychain at night. This part is my best explanation of the \"Not logged in\" error, not something I could check from the snapshot.\n\n**Other changes to `bin/nightly-review.zsh`:**\n- It pre-approves read-only tools (Read, Grep, Glob, and `git log/show/diff`). In `-p` mode Claude can't ask for permission, so without this it couldn't run `git log` even once logged in.\n- It saves `claude`'s error output and puts the start of it in the failure message, so a note would say e.g. \"Not logged in\".\n- It sends the last 3 lines of the review, which is where the prompt asks for the phone summary, instead of the first 300 characters.\n\nThe edited script passes a syntax check, but I didn't run it. Nothing was loaded, run or sent anywhere, and the plist and `notify.sh` are unchanged. Once the env file exists, test it with `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1447,"cache_read_input_tokens":24459,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1447},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07c90268-61c0-494c-ac2f-d653efc58551","uuid":"6fa4ee4e-1638-4620-ae62-54588b8c78cf","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:35:00.530Z","request_id":"req_011CgApFX8DyiqRwWrSMSnb6"}
